{"message":"Yes. For your travel pattern, my top recommendation is the personal Bluest Account—if you can meet its funding requirements. It charges no Rho fee for foreign ATM withdrawals and automatically rebates eligible ATM-operator fees up to $50 per month. You do not need to enroll or submit receipts. The Bluest Account also has a $1,500 daily ATM withdrawal limit.

Important limits: the $50 monthly cap applies to total eligible rebates, and ATM operators may still charge surcharges. When offered a currency choice, select the local currency rather than dynamic currency conversion.

Bluest requires a $75,000 opening deposit and a $112,500 minimum daily balance to maintain its benefits. If those amounts don’t fit your situation, tell me roughly how much you’d keep in the second checking account and I’ll recommend a more practical alternative."}
